# Response headers for brand.ijosh.com. Pages applies these to static assets.
#
# Five minutes everywhere: the paths are unversioned, and a redraw must reach every
# consumer without any of them redeploying. Bandwidth is unlimited on Pages, so there is
# no reason to cache harder.
#
# /mark/* carries no X-Robots-Tag on purpose. ijosh.com's favicon candidates live there,
# and Google requires that Googlebot-Image be able to crawl a favicon it is to use.
# Whether it would still use a noindex image is undocumented; the favicon is the reason
# this origin exists, so it is not risked. The index page and the photos are noindex --
# a search for the name should return ijosh.com, not this.

/
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/photo/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/mark/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
